# Homarr Provider

Manages resources in a [Homarr](https://homarr.dev) dashboard instance through its
OpenAPI-compatible REST API.

## Compatibility

**Provider 0.3.1** is built and verified against **Homarr 2.5.2**. Every feature
works from Homarr **2.3.0**. Homarr 2.0–2.2 work too, except for the features
below that need a newer Homarr; each one's page says so. The provider warns when
Homarr reports a major version other than 2.

| Provider | Verified against | Supported Homarr | Terraform |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 0.3.1 | Homarr 2.5.2 | 2.3.0 and newer 2.x; 2.0–2.2 with the exceptions below | 1.9+ |
| 0.3.0 | Homarr 2.4.1 | 2.3.0 and newer 2.x; 2.0–2.2 with the exceptions below | 1.9+ |
| 0.2.0 | Homarr 1.76.2 | 1.x; not tested against 2.x | 1.9+ |
| 0.1.0 | Homarr 1.73.0 | 1.x; not tested against 2.x | 1.9+ |

| Feature | Needs |
| --- | --- |
| `homarr_integration_connection` | Homarr 2.1.0 |
| `homarr_root_certificate` | Homarr 2.2.0 |
| Drift detection in `homarr_board_settings`, and its data source | Homarr 2.3.0 |
| `is_home` or `is_mobile_home` set to `false` | Homarr 2.3.0 |
| Setting `homarr_user` preferences other than the home boards and search preferences; `homarr_user_preferences`; `homarr_current_user`; `header` | Homarr 2.3.0 |
| `password_wo` on `homarr_user` | Terraform 1.11 |
| Import by resource identity | Terraform 1.12 |
| The `homarr_board_add_item` action; list resources for `terraform query` | Terraform 1.14 |

## What it manages

* **Apps** — `homarr_app`, and the `homarr_app` and `homarr_apps` data sources.
* **Boards** — `homarr_board`, `homarr_board_copy` (a copy of a template board,
  tiles included), `homarr_board_settings`, the `homarr_board`, `homarr_boards`
  and `homarr_board_settings` data sources, and the `homarr_board_add_item`
  action, which places a tile.
* **Users** — `homarr_user` for credentials accounts, `homarr_user_preferences`
  for any account, and the `homarr_user`, `homarr_current_user`, `homarr_users`
  and `homarr_user_preferences` data sources.
* **Invites** — `homarr_invite`, and the `homarr_invites` data source.
* **Instance** — `homarr_server_board_settings` and its data source,
  `homarr_root_certificate`, `homarr_integration_connection` and `homarr_info`.

## Scope and limitations

Homarr exposes two APIs: a stable, OpenAPI-documented REST surface under `/api/…`
and an internal tRPC surface under `/api/trpc/…`. This provider only uses the
former, because the tRPC layer is an implementation detail of the Homarr web UI
and changes without notice.

That boundary determines what can be managed. **Integrations cannot be listed
or managed over REST, and groups, search engines and API keys have no REST
surface at all, so none of them are available here.** Of the few integration
and certificate endpoints REST does offer, the provider reads two: the
connection test of a saved integration (`homarr_integration_connection`) and the
metadata of a trusted root certificate (`homarr_root_certificate`).

**Board layouts and tiles can be written over REST but never read.** Tiles can
be added, moved and resized, and a whole board rewritten in one call, but
nothing lists a board's tiles or deletes one, and layouts can only be rewritten
with the mobile layout's id, which no REST response contains. A resource built on
that could never converge on a desired state, so tiles are placed by the
`homarr_board_add_item` action instead, and `homarr_board_copy` reproduces a
board designed in the UI; see
[homarr-labs/homarr#6435](https://github.com/homarr-labs/homarr/issues/6435).

Within the REST surface, a few endpoints are write-only or create-only; each
affected attribute says so in its own documentation, and the most consequential
cases are:

| Limitation | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| Per-board settings readable only since Homarr 2.3.0 | On older Homarr, `homarr_board_settings` cannot detect drift; state reflects the last applied configuration |
| Column count absent from board responses | `homarr_board.column_count` forces replacement when changed and needs a composite import id |
| Board items cannot be read or deleted | Tiles are placed by the `homarr_board_add_item` action, not managed as a resource, and never removed by Terraform |
| Group membership not readable | `homarr_user.group_ids` is create-only; adding or removing a group forces replacement |
| A user's email cannot be cleared | Removing `homarr_user.email` forces replacement; setting or changing it happens in place |
| LDAP and OIDC accounts refuse profile changes | `homarr_user` manages credentials accounts only; use `homarr_user_preferences` for the others |
| Passwords not readable | A password changed outside Terraform is not detected as drift |
| Invite tokens returned once | `homarr_invite.token` cannot be recovered after creation or by import |

What Homarr would need to add to lift these limits is listed item by item in the
repository's
[`UPSTREAM.md`](https://github.com/rfdrew/terraform-provider-homarr/blob/main/UPSTREAM.md).

## Authentication

Create an API key in the Homarr UI under **Management > Tools > API**. Keys are
`<id>.<token>` pairs, never expire, and carry the permissions of the user that
created them — managing users, invites and server settings requires an admin.

Prefer the environment over configuration so the key stays out of your state and
version control:

```shell
export HOMARR_URL="https://homarr.example.com"
export HOMARR_API_KEY="abc123def456.xyz789tokenvalue"
```

